cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Rein, its models or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "Rein: Typed Rule Decisions that Steer Small Language Models Driving Game NPCs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Macedo
    given-names: Jasiel
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-09
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jasielmacedo/rein"
url: "https://huggingface.co/jmc0/Rein-NPC-4B"
keywords:
  - language models
  - game NPCs
  - tool calling
  - rule following
  - typed decisions
  - soft prompts
  - llama.cpp
abstract: >-
  Rein is a typed decision layer that reads rules written in plain text, returns a calibrated probability for every
  option of every rule, and turns those decisions into actions on a chat model's reply. Rein-r1 is a separate decider
  on a truncated Qwen3.5-Base backbone. Rein-NPC puts the decider inside the chat model's own checkpoint as 64 soft
  tokens in spare rows of the frozen Qwen3.5-4B embedding table, read from the next-token logits of lettered options,
  and ships as one standard GGUF that talks and decides.
